# Phase 18 P18-V01 rebalance membership no-result semantics — 2026-10-21T16:00:22Z

Branch: `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`
Starting code revision: `659ec260` (`fix(consumer): map push implementation factory setter`)
Pinned Java source: `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.

## Source finding and change

Pinned `RebalanceImpl.rebalanceByTopic` initializes `balanced=true`. If
`findConsumerIdList` returns null or an empty list, that branch logs and skips
allocation without changing the result or existing queue assignments. If the
lookup throws, `doRebalance` catches the exception and marks a non-retry-topic
pass unbalanced.

Rust had treated both null and empty membership results as unbalanced. The
clustering path now preserves the Java default result for those two no-result
cases; transport/RPC errors still mark the pass unbalanced. The membership
churn regression now covers both null and empty results while verifying that
assignments remain in place. `unavailable_membership_keeps_the_previous_queue_assignment`
continues to verify the thrown lookup-error retry path.

